/*Q19. Write a Java program that takes a string as input and outputs the reverse of that string.
Input Format:
• A single line of input contains a string. The string may contain alphabets, digits, and special characters.
Output Format:
• The output is the reversed string.*/
import java.util.Scanner;
 
public class Reverse {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);
        String s = sc.nextLine();
        String rev = "";
        for (int i = s.length() - 1; i >= 0; i--) {
            rev += s.charAt(i);
        }
        System.out.println(rev);
        sc.close();
    }
}
